(beyond its stated range.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. OCCURRENCE AND THE DEGREE CONDITION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(DKSS proves S\(7\)=Primes\(23\). A quadratic extension of a septic field) Tj T*
(preserves its torsion and has exact degree 14. This supplies all primes) Tj T*
(through 23.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For each of 29,31,37,41,43 the file occurrences.json records an irreducible) Tj T*
(polynomial f of degree 14 and rational functions x=a,y=g\(a\)/h\(a\), where) Tj T*
(f\(a\)=0. Set) Tj T*
( r=\(x^2*y-x*y+y-1\)/\(x^2*y-x\), s=\(x*y-y+1\)/\(x*y\),) Tj T*
( b=r*s*\(r-1\), c=s*\(r-1\).) Tj T*
(Then E: Y^2+\(1-c\)XY-bY=X^3-bX^2, P=\(0,0\), is an exact occurrence:) Tj T*
(verify_occurrences.m proves irreducibility, nonsingularity, P nonzero,) Tj T*
(and p*P=0 for every indicated prime p.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The degree-14 places at 37,41,43 come from van Hoeij's explicit tables.) Tj T*
(For example the x-coordinate at 41 is a root of) Tj T*
( x^14-8x^13+21x^12-11x^11-43x^10+61x^9+24x^8-80x^7) Tj T*
( +x^6+56x^5-4x^4-23x^3+5x+1.) Tj T*
(All coordinates, including y, are retained in the certificate packet.) Tj T*
(The examples at 29 and 31 were found by explicit specializations of the) Tj T*
(Sutherland--van Hoeij models. Their exact verification does not rely on) Tj T*
(Hilbert irreducibility or on existence in a different degree.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Conversely, a prime dividing E\(K\)_tors occurs as the order of a K-rational) Tj T*
(point. The resulting noncuspidal point on X_1\(p\) has degree dividing 14.) Tj T*
(For p>43, the possibilities 1,2,7 are excluded by the known classifications.) Tj T*
(It therefore has degree 14. Write D for its irreducible rational trace) Tj T*
(divisor. This is precisely the S_new\(14\) condition in Derickx--Stoll.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. THE DYADIC GLOBAL BOUND) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We use the previously proved dyadic doubling argument, with an explicit) Tj T*
(coefficient certificate replacing the coarse polynomial estimate.) Tj T*
(Let J=J_0\(p\), T its integral Hecke algebra, e the winding element,) Tj T*
(I=Ann_T\(e\), and A=J/IJ the optimal winding quotient. The group A\(Q\)) Tj T*
(is finite. Put) Tj T*
( M=H^0\(X_0\(p\)_{Z_2},Omega^1\)[I], L=pi^*Cot\(A_{Z_2}\).) Tj T*
(The integral coefficient pairing identifies M with the Z_2-dual of) Tj T*
(\(T/I\) tensor Z_2. Raynaud's theorem gives) Tj T*
(                         2M subset L subset M.) Tj T*
(No equality L=M is assumed. The earlier dyadic theorem, reproduced) Tj T*
(in the packet, gives the precise lattice argument and references.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Take m=28 and M0=157. Put) Tj T*
( T'_n=sum_{a|n} mu\(n/a\)T_a, L_n=T'_\(2n\)-2*T'_n.) Tj T*
